[{"location":"jcc/#Joint-probability-functions","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Joint probability functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"jcc/#Computing-probability-functions","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Computing probability functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"jcc/","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Joint Chance Contraints","text":"compute_with_QMC","category":"page"},{"location":"jcc/#ChanceConstraints.compute_with_QMC","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"ChanceConstraints.compute_with_QMC","text":"    compute_with_QMC(j, κ, Σ, μ; two_sided=false, s=10_000, rng=MersenneTwister(1234))\n\nCompute a quasi-Monte Carlo (QMC) approximation of a joint probability and its gradient.\n\nLet xi be a random vector with mean mu and covariance matrix Sigma. For the indices i = j ldots j+kappa, the one-sided probability is\n\nf(x) = mathbbPbigl(x_i geq xi_i i = j ldots j+kappabigr)\n\nWhen two_sided=true, the probability is computed using the corresponding two-sided inequalities.\n\nReturns (f, ∇f), where f is the estimated probability and ∇f is its gradient with respect to x. The gradient is computed using the Prékopa theorem, as described in Section X.\n\nArguments\n\nj::Integer: Starting index of the components in Sigma and mu.\nκ::Integer: Number of additional components. The joint event includes indices j ldots j+kappa.\nΣ::AbstractMatrix: Covariance matrix of xi.\nμ::AbstractVector: Mean vector of xi.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ntwo_sided::Bool=false: Whether to use two-sided inequalities.\ns::Integer=10_000: Number of QMC samples.\nrng=MersenneTwister(1234): Random number generator for sampling. The fixed default seed makes estimates repeatable across solver iterations, which can help optimization converge. For standalone probability evaluation with a non-fixed random source, pass RandomDevice().\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"jcc/","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Joint Chance Contraints","text":"compute_with_SRD","category":"page"},{"location":"jcc/#ChanceConstraints.compute_with_SRD","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"ChanceConstraints.compute_with_SRD","text":"    compute_with_SRD(w, κ, transformed_samples, μ)\n\nCompute a spherical radial decomposition (SRD) approximation of a joint probability and its gradient.\n\nFor the indices i = w ldots w+kappa, the probability is\n\nf(x) = mathbbPbigl(x_i geq xi_i i = w ldots w+kappabigr)\n\nwhere the random-variable samples used in the SRD calculation are provided by transformed_samples, and mu is the mean vector.\n\nReturns (f, ∇f), where f is the estimated probability and ∇f is its gradient with respect to x. The gradient is computed using the Prékopa theorem, as described in Section X.\n\nArguments\n\nw::Integer: Starting index of the components in the joint event.\nκ::Integer: Number of additional components in the event; the event covers indices w ldots w+kappa.\ntransformed_samples::AbstractMatrix: Transformed samples used by the SRD calculation.\nμ::AbstractVector: Mean vector used in the probability calculation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"jcc/#Adding-chance-constraints-to-a-JuMP-model","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Adding chance constraints to a JuMP model","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"jcc/","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Joint Chance Contraints","text":"add_JCC_QMC","category":"page"},{"location":"jcc/#ChanceConstraints.add_JCC_QMC","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"ChanceConstraints.add_JCC_QMC","text":"    add_JCC_QMC(m, x, idx, κ, Σ, μ, p; two_sided=false, s=10_000, rng=MersenneTwister(1234))\n\nAdd a system of joint chance constraints to a JuMP model.\n\nFor each starting index j in textttidx, the added constraint is\n\nmathbbPbigl(x_i geq xi_i i = j ldots j+kappabigr) geq p\n\nwhere xi is a random vector with mean mu and covariance matrix Sigma. When two_sided=true, the probability uses the corresponding two-sided inequalities.\n\nThe probability is approximated using quasi-Monte Carlo (QMC). The function registers it as a user-defined operator in the JuMP model and supplies the gradient computed by compute_with_QMC.\n\nArguments\n\nm::JuMP.Model: JuMP model to which the constraints are added.\nx::AbstractVector: Decision variables used in the constraints.\nidx::AbstractArray: Starting indices of the reliability windows.\nκ::Integer: Number of additional components in each window; each probability covers indices j ldots j+kappa.\nΣ::AbstractMatrix: Covariance matrix of xi.\nμ::AbstractArray: Mean vector of xi.\np::Float64: Minimum required probability level.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ntwo_sided::Bool=false: Whether to use two-sided inequalities.\ns::Integer=10_000: Number of QMC samples.\nrng=MersenneTwister(1234): Random number generator for QMC sampling. The fixed default seed makes estimates repeatable across solver iterations, which can help optimization converge. For standalone probability evaluation with a non-fixed random source, pass RandomDevice().\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"jcc/","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"Joint Chance Contraints","text":"add_JCC_SRD","category":"page"},{"location":"jcc/#ChanceConstraints.add_JCC_SRD","page":"Joint Chance Contraints","title":"ChanceConstraints.add_JCC_SRD","text":"    add_JCC_SRD(model, x, idx, κ, Σ, μ, p; s=100_000, seed=1234)\n\nAdd a system of joint chance constraints to a JuMP model using spherical radial decomposition (SRD).\n\nFor each starting index j in textttidx, the added constraint is\n\nmathbbPbigl(x_i geq xi_i i = j ldots j+kappabigr) geq p\n\nwhere xi is a random vector with mean mu and covariance matrix Sigma.\n\nThe probability is computed using compute_with_SRD. The function registers it as a user-defined operator in the JuMP model and supplies its gradient, also computed using compute_with_SRD.\n\nArguments\n\nmodel::JuMP.Model: JuMP model to which the constraints are added.\nx::AbstractVector: Decision variables used in the constraints.\nidx::AbstractVector: Starting indices of the reliability windows.\nκ::Integer: Number of additional components in each window; each probability covers indices j ldots j+kappa.\nΣ::AbstractMatrix: Covariance matrix of xi.\nμ::AbstractVector: Mean vector of xi.\np::Real: Minimum required probability level.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ns::Integer=100_000: Number of samples used by the SRD computation.\nseed::Integer=1234: Seed used for the random-number generation. The default makes the estimates repeatable across solver iterations, which can help optimization converge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"examples/#Examples","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/#First-example","page":"Examples","title":"First example","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"Newsvendor with Individual Chance Constraint \nNewsvendor with Joint Chance Constraint","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Second-example","page":"Examples","title":"Second example","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"Financial portfolio ICC \nFinancial portfolio JCC","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Third-Example","page":"Examples","title":"Third Example","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"Hydropower Dispatch ICC \nHydropower Dispatch JCC","category":"page"},{"location":"icc/#Individual-probability-functions","page":"Individual Chance Contraints","title":"Individual probability functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#JointChance.jl","page":"Home","title":"JointChance.jl","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"A package for dealing with Joint Chance Constraints in Julia.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Pages = [\"index.md\"]","category":"page"},{"location":"#Install","page":"Home","title":"Install","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"# pkg> add \"https://github.com/naouess/JointChance\"","category":"page"},{"location":"#Resources-for-getting-started","page":"Home","title":"Resources for getting started","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Here some math stuff \nSome JuMP and Julia stuff \nRefer to our paper in Annals of OR","category":"page"},{"location":"#The-math-behind-it-all","page":"Home","title":"The math behind it all","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Here we explain Chance constraints ","category":"page"}]
